FlClash for iOS
===============

This repository is a fork of FlClash (github.com/chen08209/FlClash, GPL-3.0),
imported from github.com/hyy807/FlClash at version 0.9.2, with an iOS port
added.

GPL-3.0 obligations: the complete corresponding source of every binary this
repository builds is this repository, including the mihomo core submodule
(core/Clash.Meta) and the Rust helper (plugins/rust_api).

iOS host layer
--------------

The Swift/Objective-C iOS host in ios/ and the C callback table
(core/bride.h, core/cmd/ios/bride.c) are derived from the iOS work published in
chenx-dust/FlClash-Patched (GPL-3.0), which is itself derived from FlClash:

  * ios/NECore/PacketTunnelProvider.swift
  * ios/NECore/PacketTunnelNetworkConfiguration.swift  (descriptor scan)
  * ios/NECore/NECoreBridge.{h,m}, ios/Runner/IOSCoreBridge.{h,m}
  * ios/NECore/NECoreEventQueue.swift
  * ios/Runner/{Tunnel,Core,Storage,Shared}/**, Widget/**
  * core/bride.h, core/bride.c

Changes made here, relative to that source:

  * the Go bridge is a separate `package main` (core/cmd/ios) that imports the
    0.9.2 core package, instead of living inside the core package;
  * the Dart-facing channel contract follows FlClash 0.9.2, which splits
    `<bundle>/core` (method calls, bytes) from `<bundle>/service` (lifecycle)
    and sends a command revision with start/stop;
  * the memory governor (phys_footprint sampling, lowmem archive and
    setMemoryLimit export) is new;
  * the Xcode core build phase calls tool/ios/build_core.sh instead of the
    upstream Dart build harness;
  * bundle identifiers, App Group and display name are FlClash's.

Prior art consulted for the architecture (not copied):

  * SagerNet/sing-box — clients/apple-ios, the packet-tunnel + c-archive shape;
  * Apple NetworkExtension documentation for NEPacketTunnelProvider,
    NEPacketTunnelNetworkSettings and NEProvider lifecycle;
  * MetaCubeX/mipstack — mihomo's userspace stack, the fallback when no fd is
    available.
